{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>As an eagle stirs up his nest.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory (Sifrei) expounded what they expounded (see Rashi z\"l), and besides their words it is explained according to the statement of Amram z\"l (Leviticus Rabbah 17:4) that when Israel transgress His will, the Master of Justice does not touch lives first, but begins to rouse them with afflictions of houses, then with afflictions of garments, and so forth — and this is the verse ״כְּנֶשֶׁר יָעִיר קִנּוֹ״: likewise HaShem stirs His children. He also stirs them according to the capacity they are able to withstand, as they said z\"l (Genesis Rabbah 55:2) that HaShem tests a person only with a measure that he can bear." "<b>And it says</b> ״he spreads his wings״ etc. — according to their statement (Sifrei Deuteronomy 3:29): His right hand is outstretched to receive those who return, for if through the stirring that HaShem rouses for Israel they awaken to return in repentance, immediately His right hand is outstretched. And it says ״he spreads״ in the future tense — this is its measure: the reason he will spread his wings from the outset is in order to take up the Jewish person who returns in repentance, for without this he would not have spread his wings." "<b>He bears him on his pinions</b> – and it says ״he bears him״ etc. — according to the statement of our Rabbis of blessed memory (Tikkunei Zohar, Tikkun 70, 131a) on the verse (Ecclesiastes 10:20) ״and a possessor of wings will tell the matter,״ for there is a certain order of angels called possessors of wings, and their service is that every good utterance and blessing of HaShem that proceeds from the mouth of a Jew — their wings bear it up. And this is what it says ״he bears him on his pinion״ — meaning, he bears what comes from him, from the good."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:19.812046760Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}